# Regenerated by every `mutmut run`; it is build output, not source.
mutants/
.mutmut-cache

# Playwright end-to-end artifacts (traces, videos, banked storage state)
e2e/.artifacts/

# What the deploy wrote on the host — a record of a deploy, not source.
#
# It was tracked once, and that made it a lie in both directions. `git archive`
# carries tracked files, so every deploy unpacked a committed SHA over the
# host's own record of what it is running — the file infra/deploy.sh calls "the
# only trustworthy record" and then reads, one line later, for the deletion
# sweep. And on a checkout it gave readBuildInfo() a stale `source: 'file'` to
# report, where the absence it is designed for reports `unknown` instead.
BUILD_SHA
RELEASES
